  "solution": {
    "text": "As <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>(</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>)</mo></math> is a point on <math><mn>3</mn><mi>x</mi><mi>&#160;</mi><mo>&#8211;</mo><mi>&#160;</mi><mn>4</mn><mi>y</mi><mi>&#160;</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>&#160;</mi><mn>7</mn><mi>&#160;</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>&#160;</mi><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo></math> the rotation is possible.<br /><br />Slope of the given line <math><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>3</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>4</mn></mrow></mfrac></math><br /><br />Slope of the line in its new position <math><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mn>3</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>4</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>3</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>4</mn></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mo>-</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>7</mn></mrow></mfrac></math><br /><br />Therefore, the required equation is <math><mi>y</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>=</mo><mo>-</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>7</mn></mrow></mfrac><mi>&#160;</mi><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfenced></math> or <math><mn>7</mn><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>6</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math>"
  }
}